==Trivia==
*The Japanese name of this stage, Oreore-sagi, is a pun and reference to ''Oreore-sagi'' (オレオレ詐欺), a type of phone scam where the caller starts by saying, "''Ore, ore''" (オレオレ, "It's me! It's me!"), which is supposed to trick the victim into thinking a distressed relative is on the other end. The joke is that the stage's name is spelled with サギ, meaning "heron", instead of 詐欺, meaning "fraud".
**This also implies that the "call" in the stage's English name is in fact a phone call.
*Prior to the [[Version 11.1 Update]], [[Sir Rel]] spawned infinitely.

